TIP:  As is often the case, when entering the chorus, and playing lines within the chorus, the chord change for the next line comes in early, and is depicted at the end of the previous line, e.g. the  (G)  --> (C)  and  (G)  --> (D).

TIP:  You can just ignore those intro notes, but if you want to play them (or just you’re just learning to incorporate fills) pick the open 4th string <d>, then fret the 4th string with the finger of your choice (I use the index) and pick the 4th string <e> followed by the open 3rd string right below it:  <d> - <e> - <g>.  The same set of notes are (can be) picked when moving between the chords.

TIP:  Can also be played using (A), (D), and (E), capo’d at the 1st fret.  Intro notes would be <e>, <f#>, and <a>.
 
      

